    "notes": "Relation5636139/Q2390563 establishes the flared footprint; named current PMTiles bridge35184750129947 establishes the traffic crossing axis. Anchor[30.313628911972046,59.92582028905424], heading2.0450069232296695: +X NNW/Stolyarny Lane, -X SSE/Kokushkin Lane, +Z ENE. Corrected the old0.381882rad rectangle long side, which follows the broad flared width rather than the road. Road extent19.004823m is separate from the catalog18.92m length. Clear span15m, width13.1m and shear0.08 remain photo/map reconstruction controls. Geographic fit rejected and canonical placement remains draft. Standard Mapzen z14 and z15 both contain a steep bank rise. At z15, native water is16.923998m; the source road is about20.50m while southeast landing ground rises to25–30m and beyond. The unchanged-terrain fixture buries part of the source and retains the original procedural bridge. Some diagnostic cameras are below the noisy terrain; they are not placement evidence. An isolated test of existing road replacement, connected approaches and capped terrain exposes the bridge but leaves cliffs/holes and missing approach-width coverage. It is also rejected. No distorted bridge, fabricated steep ramp or canonical terrain change was used to claim readiness."
